 "notes": "Libretto by Emanuel Schikaneder (1791). Words as printed in the Edition Peters vocal score, which the app follows where it differs from the libretto: \"Es zeigen die Pforten\" (the libretto has \"Doch zeigen\"), \"in dem Weisheitstempel\" (\"in der Weisheit Tempel\"), Tamino's \"Sarastro wohnet hier?\" as a question, \"So gieb\" (\"Nun gib\"), \"das Gram und Jammer\" (\"die\"), \"jetzund\" (\"itzund\"), and the old spellings \"Thätigkeit\", \"Müssiggang\", \"muthig\", \"Thür\", \"Heiligthum\", \"Eigenthum\", \"thut\", \"Räthsel\", \"theurer\", \"gieb\". The music's repeats are kept: \"Paminen retten\" twice, Tamino's \"Zurück! Zurück!\", \"Bald, bald, bald\", \"sie lebt? sie lebt?\" and \"hier, hier\" in the last line. The singer the print calls \"Priester\" is the Speaker. The offstage voice that calls \"Zurück!\" (bars 32 and 39, printed on Tamino's staff) and the offstage chorus (tenors and basses, from bar 105) are heard with the piano and have no phrases here. IPA follows sung German stage diction: final -er, -ern as [ɐ]; the prefixes er-, ver-, zer- with [ɛr]; r elsewhere rolled or flipped; ch as [ç] after front vowels and [x] after back vowels; glottal stops [ʔ] before initial vowels; final b d g devoiced.",
